      "math_academy_id": "e-4979",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218586/assets/303b6a70330995c124cdfea0bc125febd5ebcf80cb79c8656086d57f3a6f272f.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Sketch the graph of $y = \\dfrac{1}{2}f(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "To graph the function $y = \\dfrac{1}{2}f(x),$ we take the graph of $y = f(x)$ and compress it by factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of dividing the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y = f(x)$ by $2.$\n\nThe resulting graph is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218586/assets/71b6584d644419a56b2cebb64124510e9f15cca8a4f19e6c1a8d4b6f1441cd0a.png)",
